nodecode-pstack is a rewrite of Cloeille's Cloeille/pstack:

  https://github.com/Cloeille/pstack
  commit d9454cc1ecba5f28b136deacdfe2df959cf7cdec
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 poteto (adapted by Madeleine) (LICENSE)

prose/skills/ is the original's skills/ folder, unchanged: poteto-mode with
its 17 playbooks, the 51 other skills, and the references and scripts they
name. The cell around it is new: where the original is a Hermes plugin whose
register() reads every SKILL.md's frontmatter and hands the lot to Hermes's
skill loader, this is one Lisp cell that lists the same files itself (each
skill's own description line, each playbook's opening bolded line) behind a
`pstack` tool and a /pstack command, and reads one file when it is asked for.
A served file keeps the original's words and carries two lines above them:
where it sits, and how the original's skill_view(name='pstack:X',
file_path='playbooks/Y.md') reads here, as pstack(name="X") and
pstack(name="Y"). The prose is not otherwise edited, so the Hermes names it
still uses (skill_view, delegate_task, cronjob, session_search, and the
scripts/watch-pr and references/bugbot-triage.md that the original repository
names but does not ship) are explained in the header rather than rewritten.

Left out, and why: the repository's docs/ folder (a guide to the original's
own plugin layout, not to the playbooks), scripts/check_refs.py and
scripts/check_version.py (the original's maintainer tooling, run by hand, not
by the plugin), and plugin.yaml (the Hermes manifest, which the cell's .asd
replaces). Hermes's skill frontmatter keys other than name and description
(version, author, licence, platforms, tags) are read by nobody here: a
Nodecode cell carries its own metadata in the .asd, and the catalogue needs
only a name and the one line that says when to read the file.
